{"absolutePath":"P11_Inner.sol","exportedSymbols":{"P11_Inner":[48]},"id":49,"license":"MIT","nodeType":"SourceUnit","nodes":[{"id":1,"literals":["solidity","^","0.8",".20"],"nodeType":"PragmaDirective","src":"32:24:0"},{"abstract":false,"baseContracts":[],"canonicalName":"P11_Inner","contractDependencies":[],"contractKind":"contract","documentation":{"id":2,"nodeType":"StructuredDocumentation","src":"58:1165:0","text":"ISOLATES: internal-call inlining and what it does to PATH IDENTITY.\n `outer` calls `inner`, and `inner` has its own branch. The pass physically\n inlines the callee before enumerating, so `inner`'s decision becomes part of\n `outer`'s path identity: `outer` should enumerate 2 x 2 = 4 complete paths,\n not 2.\n EXPECTED: `instrumented 4 complete path(s) across 1 unit(s)` with an\n expansion factor of 2.00x, and every path's decision sequence containing\n BOTH the outer and the inner decision.\n WHY THIS ONE IS LOAD-BEARING: internal-call expansion multiplied aqua's path\n count by 72.97x and farming's by 381.44x. That multiplication is the single\n largest driver of how many claims a run has to solve, and it has never been\n observed on a contract where the right answer can be counted by hand. Here\n it is 4, and anything else is a defect rather than a benchmark property.\n It is also the shape behind the double-identity hazard: a body reachable\n both as a unit and as an inlined callee. `inner` is `internal`, so it is not\n a unit \u2014 the variant where the callee is PUBLIC is a separate contract."},"fullyImplemented":true,"id":48,"linearizedBaseContracts":[48],"name":"P11_Inner","nameLocation":"1232:9:0","nodeType":"ContractDefinition","nodes":[{"constant":false,"functionSelector":"51f91066","id":4,"mutability":"mutable","name":"tag","nameLocation":"1263:3:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":48,"src":"1248:18:0","stateVariable":true,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"},"typeN